# Static-host fallback (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify syntax).
#
# vite-ssg prerenders the six indexable routes to real HTML, and the host serves those files
# directly — this rule only applies when no file matches. It covers the two routes that are
# deliberately not prerendered:
#   /settings          noIndex, so the app shell rendering it client-side costs nothing
#   anything unknown   renders the app's own not-found view instead of the host's 404 page
#
# Both are noIndex, so returning 200 here does not put a soft 404 in the index.
/*  /index.html  200
